DQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86886444?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221","html_url":"https://github.com/Niko1221","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Niko1221/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-03T01:19:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-03T01:19:23Z","body":"Agreed, this would help on shared desktops, and #560 / #516 show the same problem on Linux. Keeping it open as planned work. The plan:\n\n1. Allocate the expert cache in segments (e.g. 1 GiB each) instead of one block, so part of it can be freed. The coldest segments by profile rank go first.\n2. An opt-in engine command between requests, `VRAM <reserve_mib>`, that shrinks the cache to leave that much free and grows it back when the VRAM is free again. The adaptive tier re-warms the returned experts.\n3. A server endpoint (`POST /v1/vram {\"reserve_mib\": 8192}`) and a config default, so a script or a hotkey can switch before a game or CAD session.\n\nIt would never shrink or grow on its own. For now the static `--vram-reserve-mib N` (0.1.37) is the way to leave room for another app.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Niko1221/Strata/issues/comments/5964032377/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]